1. What this covers.
   This licence covers the Civic-Chain Grant & Budget Auditor engine, its
   skill package, its rulesets, and all accompanying files in this repository
   published at or after the v1.0.0 tag, which is the licence cut-over recorded
   in CHANGELOG.md. Everything published before that tag (the 0.x history, up to
   and including commit 88e08a3, the last version offered under MIT) was offered
   under the MIT Licence and remains available to anyone who already holds it
   under those MIT terms. This licence does not revoke any MIT grant already
   made.

   This licence governs the software however the licensee obtains it, including
   when an AI agent installs it from a package registry (for example npm) or a
   source repository at the direction of a skill, and whether or not that skill
   was obtained through a third-party marketplace. A marketplace's own terms
   govern the delivery of the skill text; this licence governs the installed
   software itself.

2. Grant.
   Subject to an active Civic-Chain subscription, Civic-Chain grants a
   non-exclusive, non-transferable right to install and run the software on the
   licensee's own systems, for the licensee's auditing purposes, including
   auditing the books of the licensee's clients under a professional engagement.
   This right is perpetual as to any version of the software released to the
   licensee while the subscription was active: the licensee may continue to run
   those versions after the subscription lapses. An active subscription is
   required to receive new versions, updates, and rulesets, and to use any
   hosted or marketplace (MCP) delivery of the software.

3. Source-available, not open source.
   The source is published so that the licensee may inspect it. Inspection does
   not grant any right to redistribute, resell, sublicense, publish, or create
   derivative works for distribution. "Open source" is not an accurate
   description of this licence and must not be used for it.

4. No redistribution or resale.
   (a) The licensee may not distribute, resell, rent, lease, or make the
   software available to any third party, whether modified or unmodified. Under
   a professional engagement (Section 2) the licensee may produce and share the
   software's reports and findings with the client being audited, but may not
   give the client the software itself.

   (b) AI model providers. Nothing in this Section prevents the licensee from
   transmitting the software's skill instructions, rulesets, prompts, queries,
   or data to a third-party AI model provider (for example Anthropic, OpenAI, or
   Google) solely to execute the licensee's own workflows with the software,
   provided the provider is not permitted to train on, fine-tune from, or retain
   the transmitted content beyond what is necessary to return a response.

   (c) No AI training or competing use. The licensee may not use the software,
   its skill package, rulesets, prompts, or outputs to train, fine-tune, or
   evaluate any machine-learning model, or to build, train, or improve any
   product or agent skill that competes with the software.

5. No warranty.
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NONINFRINGEMENT.

6. Limitation of liability.
   IN NO EVENT SHALL CIVIC-CHAIN BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER
   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
