   SOFTWARE.

7. Not a professional audit opinion.
   The software's outputs are produced by software. They are not an audit, an
   attestation, or a professional opinion of any kind, and are not a substitute
   for review by a qualified accountant or auditor.

8. Termination.
   On lapse of the subscription, the licensee stops receiving new versions,
   updates, rulesets, and support, and the rights that require an active
   subscription under Section 2 end; the perpetual right to run versions already
   received during an active subscription continues.

   This licence terminates automatically, independent of subscription status, if
   the licensee breaches Section 3 (source-available restrictions) or Section 4
   (redistribution, resale, AI training, or competing use). On such termination
   the licensee must cease all use of the software and delete all copies in their
   possession or control.

9. Governing law and venue.
   This licence is governed by the laws of the State of Maine, without regard to
   conflict-of-law principles. Any dispute arising out of this licence must be
   brought exclusively in the state or federal courts located in Cumberland
   County, Maine.
